---
/*
 * This route used to cross-product every city x every entry in a local
 * BLOG_SLUGS list, generating /locations/<city>/<article-slug>/ for all of
 * them -- 7 cities x 30 slugs = 210 pages. Several of those slugs already
 * name a DIFFERENT city ("tesla-wall-connector-installation-bend-or",
 * "ev-charger-installation-salem-or" -- Salem isn't even a served city), so
 * every one of those pages had two different geo-targets baked into its own
 * title: confirmed live, e.g. /locations/redmond/tesla-wall-connector-installation-bend-or/
 * rendered "Tesla Wall Connector Installation Bend OR in Redmond, OR".
 *
 * They were also pure duplicates: the real, correctly city-agnostic version
 * of every one of these articles already exists at the canonical root
 * /<article-slug>/ (src/pages/[slug].astro). This route added nothing but
 * 210 self-contradictory copies of content that already existed correctly
 * elsewhere.
 *
 * getStaticPaths returns nothing on purpose, so this route builds zero
 * pages. Every one of the 210 old URLs 301s to its real canonical article --
 * see public/_redirects, the "Cannibalized per-city article duplicates"
 * block -- so nothing that was indexed just disappears.
 *
 * The real, legitimate per-city equivalent is
 * src/pages/locations/[city]/services/[service].astro, which is correctly
 * localized (real per-city schema, real per-city copy) and is untouched.
 */
export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [];
}
---
